@format 1
@id media-loading.in-merge
@title In Merge
@section Media loading
@area In Merge
@entry merge-group-drop, merge-items-add
@summary Show Merge-specific program intake: group-area drops first load paths into Files, and newly loaded Files entries can trigger automatic group rebuilding.
@related media-loading.common.files-intake, media-loading.common.docket-insertion, media-loading.common.file-drops
@tag media
@tag loading
@tag merge

@alias merge = Cadroue.UIShell.PMainArea.PMergeTab
@alias group = Cadroue.UIShell.PPanels.PGroup
@alias list = Cadroue.UIShell.PPanels.PList

[merge-group-drop] External file drop on Merge group <input>
~ This starts with external file drop on Merge group.
[Technical explanation]
- Receive a file-system drop on the group area or an existing group card; PGroupPathsRead invokes the Merge PGroupFileRequest delegate @ group.PGroupDropHandle(...)
  @ group.PGroupCardHandle(...)
  @ group.PGroupPathsRead(...)
> merge-group-files

[merge-items-add] Newly loaded Merge entries announced <input>
~ This starts with newly loaded Merge entries announced.
[Technical explanation]
= PListItemsAdd reaches PMergeItemsHandle after new docket entries have been inserted.
> merge-auto-result

[merge-group-files] Load dropped paths into Merge Files <process>
~ This step handles load dropped paths into Merge Files.
[Technical explanation]
- The delegate first calls PListPathsAdd, so common Files intake and Docket insertion complete synchronously; it then scans the same drop again and returns those supported paths to PGroupPathsRead for group insertion @ list.PListPathsAdd(...)
  @ list.PListMediaScan(...)
> merge-group-inserted

[merge-auto-result] Auto grouping enabled <decision>
~ The program checks auto grouping enabled.
[Technical explanation]
- PMergeItemsHandle updates automatic grouping only when the Merge group owner currently has auto grouping enabled @ merge.PMergeItemsHandle(...)
? "Auto grouping enabled" > merge-auto-update
? "Auto grouping disabled" > merge-auto-nochange

[merge-group-inserted] Dropped media loaded and grouped <output>
~ This path ends with dropped media loaded and grouped.
[Technical explanation]
= Supported dropped paths have entered the program Files docket through PListPathsAdd and are then offered to the target/new Merge group.

[merge-auto-update] Recompute automatic groups <process>
~ This step handles recompute automatic groups.
[Technical explanation]
- Rebuild automatic grouping after the new Files entries were announced @ group.PGroupAutoUpdate(...)
> merge-auto-complete

[merge-auto-nochange] Loaded entries leave grouping unchanged <output>
~ This path ends with loaded entries leave grouping unchanged.
[Technical explanation]
= PListItemsAdd causes no grouping update while auto grouping is disabled.

[merge-auto-complete] Automatic groups include loaded entries <output>
~ This path ends with automatic groups include loaded entries.
[Technical explanation]
= Merge grouping reflects the newly loaded Files entries.
